          "id": "event-120",
          "title": "AURORA - A Shiny app designed to create Darwin Core Archives from messy biodiversity datasets",
          "start": "2:00 PM",
          "end": "2:15 PM",
          "speakers": [
            "Sara Araújo"
          ],
          "abstract": "Biodiversity monitoring data are commonly stored in heterogeneous tabular formats, hindering standardisation, validation, and publication through public repositories. Researchers often face technical challenges, such as taxonomic variations and multiple date and geospatial format inconsistencies, that must be addressed before datasets can be submitted to global repositories like GBIF. To address these challenges, we developed the AURORA Shiny application that provides an intuitive, end-to-end workflow for transforming raw datasets into publication-ready Darwin Core tables. The application supports data ingestion from diverse tabular formats, enabling users to convert raw datasets into tidy data format. An interactive mapping interface allows users to align user-specific fields with Darwin Core terms by combining manual selection with automated suggestions and mandatory-field validation. The tool automates essential data-cleaning tasks for taxonomic integrity by integrating API calls to the WoRMS and GBIF Backbone Taxonomies and facilitates the use of controlled vocabulary in the Extended Measurement or Fact table. Finally, a quality control module offers diagnostics on data completeness and identifies missing key fields, providing detailed information about issues and errors for tracing and resolution. Currently, the Occurrence, Event, and extended Measurement or Fact extension DwC tables are available for export. A metadata form that follows the GBIF IPT format is provided to allow prefilling and downloading, facilitating metadata review among dataset authors. The output comprises standards-compliant DwC tables ready for publication. By streamlining these time-consuming processes into a user-friendly interface, this application reduces the technical barriers to biodiversity data mobilization and global sharing. The application is accessible to the public via a web browser by accessing https://bio-shiny.ua.pt/aurora/",
          "virtual": false,
          "cancelled": false,
          "note": "",
